{{Quote|This is where we are. And this is where the Llanic Run intersects with the Triellus Trade Route&mdash;near the planet Llanic.|[[Tomasso]]|<ref name="Free Fall">''[[Poe Dameron: Free Fall]]''</ref>}}
The '''Triellus Trade Route''' was a [[hyperspace route]] running between the astronomical objects [[Centares]] and [[Enarc]], touching a number of regions including [[Mid Rim Territories]], [[Outer Rim Territories]], [[Wild Space]], [[the Slice]], and the [[Trailing Sectors]]. It intersected with a number of other routes including the [[Perlemian Trade Route]] at Centares, the [[Corellian Run]] at the [[planet]] [[Arkanis]], the [[Salin Corridor]] at the planet [[Sy Myrth]], the [[Llanic Spice Run]] at the planet [[Llanic]] and more.

The [[Hutt Clan]] controlled the Triellus Trade Route by the time of the [[Clone Wars]], which cause problems for the [[Confederacy of Independent Systems|Separatist Alliance]] when they sided with the [[Galactic Republic]]. The route was also used as part of the [[Spice Triangle]], a trade network controlled by the [[Pyke Syndicate]] and ran between the worlds [[Tatooine]] and [[Ryloth]] and the astronomical body [[Roon]]. The smuggler [[Tryphon Leo]] wanted to lock the triangle down and toll the Triellus Trade Route's lucrative segments, but was [[Death|killed]] before he could make any of his plans possible.

==Description==
===Expanse===
The Triellus Trade Route was a circuitous [[hyperspace route]]<ref name="Collapse">''[[Collapse of the Republic]]''</ref> which ran between the astronomical objects [[Centares]] and [[Enarc]]. The route passed from the [[Mid Rim Territories]] to the [[Outer Rim Territories]] and [[Wild Space]] before passing back into the Outer Rim and Mid Rim.<ref name="TFABG">[[Star Wars: The Force Awakens Beginner Game|''Star Wars: The Force Awakens'' Beginner Game]]</ref> It also passed between the regions known as [[the Slice]] and the [[Trailing Sectors]].<ref name="Regions" /> The Triellus Trade Route passed through a number of [[sector]]s, including the [[Bheriz sector]],<ref name="RO locations" /> [[Baxel sector]],<ref name="TFABG" /> [[Galov sector]],<ref name="RO locations" /> [[Arkanis sector]],<ref name="Rise" /> and the [[Savareen sector]].<ref name="Savareen and Ku'Bakai" />

===Locations===
From Centares in the Mid Rim, the Triellus Trade Route made its way to<ref name="Galaxy Map">{{GalaxyMapPoster}}</ref> the the [[Siniteen]] [[homeworld]] of<ref name="Alien Archive">''[[Star Wars: Alien Archive]]''</ref> [[Mileva]] before passing into the Outer Rim. The route then passed to the<ref name="Galaxy Map" /> [[planet]]s<ref name="Geektionary French">''[[Star Wars: Geektionary: The Galaxy from A - Z]]'' {{C|French version only}}</ref><ref name="Nakara DB">{{Databank|naraka|Naraka}}</ref><ref name="Part IV">{{Kenobi|Part IV}} &mdash; Audio description</ref> [[Sy Myrth]], [[Naraka]],<ref name="Galaxy Map" /> and [[Jabiim]] as well as the astronomical objects [[Taskeed system|Taskeed]] and [[Dennogra]].<ref name="TFABG" /> After, it reached the [[Yarma system]]&mdash;which included the<ref name="Galaxy Map" /> planet<ref name="Steps">{{Rebels|Steps Into Shadow}}</ref> [[Yarma]]&mdash;and the<ref name="Galaxy Map" /> planet<ref name="Rebel in the Ranks">''[[Servants of the Empire: Rebel in the Ranks]]''</ref> [[Marleyvane]]<ref name="Galaxy Map" /> before making it to [[Junkfort Station]]<ref name="TFABG" /> and the<ref name="Galaxy Map" /> planets<ref name="Imperial Cadet 5">[[Han Solo - Imperial Cadet 5|''Han Solo - Imperial Cadet'' 5]]</ref><ref name="The Droid with a Heart">{{StoryCite|story=The Droid with a Heart|book=Myths & Fables}}</ref><ref name="Force Collection">{{ForceCollection|Garindan|star=2}}</ref> [[Qhulosk]],<ref name="Galaxy Map" /> [[Alamass]], and [[Kubindi]],<ref name="TFABG" /> the latter world being in the [[Ku'Bakai system]].<ref name="Savareen and Ku'Bakai" />

The Triellus Trade Route then went to the astronomical objects [[Drualkiin system|Drualkiin]] and [[Formos]] and the<ref name="BMF 29">{{BuildFalconCite|29|Guide to the Galaxy}}</ref> planet<ref name="Eadu DB">{{Databank|eadu|Eadu}}</ref> [[Eadu]] in the [[Eadu system]] before reaching<ref name="Galaxy Map" /> the edge of [[Wild Space]]<ref name="Bomber Command">''[[The Last Jedi: Bomber Command]]''</ref> at [[Aduba]].<ref name="RO locations" /> The route touched with Wild Space<ref name="Visual Encyclopedia">''[[Star Wars: The Visual Encyclopedia]]''</ref> after to the<ref name="RO locations" /> planet<ref name="Teth DB">{{Databank|teth|Teth}}</ref> [[Teth]] in the [[Teth system]] before reaching the<ref name="Galaxy Map" /> planet<ref name="Gadgets and Gear">''[[Gadgets and Gear]]''</ref> [[Barab I]],<ref name="Galaxy Map" /> the celestial body [[Dubrava system|Dubrava]], and the<ref name="TFABG" /> [[moon]]<ref name="KoF">''[[Knights of Fate]]''</ref> of [[Syvris]]. The Triellus Trade Route followed by going to the<ref name="Galaxy Map" /> planets<ref name="A&S">''[[Star Wars: Aliens and Ships of the Galaxy]]''</ref><ref name="Poe Dameron 8">[[Poe Dameron 8|''Poe Dameron'' 8]]</ref> [[Gamorr]] and [[Kaddak]], the latter located in the [[Kaddak system]], as well as the astronomical objects [[Arvina]], [[Molavar]],<ref name="Galaxy Map" /> and [[Roon]].<ref name="Smuggler's Guide" />

The Triellus Trade Route made its way to the [[Cosmatanic Steppes gas giant|gas giant]] where the [[Cosmatanic Steppes]] were found and then to the [[Tatoo system]], containing the planet [[Tatooine]], and the [[Geonosis system]], with the planet [[Geonosis]].<ref name="Rise" /> The route then went on to the<ref name="Galaxy Map" /> planets<ref name="DoR">''[[Dawn of Rebellion]]''</ref><ref name="Old Friend">{{TCW|Old Friends Not Forgotten}}</ref><ref name="Rise" /><ref name="Free Fall" /> [[Arkanis]], [[Yerbana]],<ref name="Galaxy Map" /> [[Nelvaan]], and [[Llanic]],<ref name="TFABG" /> covering the [[Arkanis system|Arkanis]] and [[Llanic system]]s.<ref name="Galaxy Map" /> The route entered the Mid Rim again after that and reached the astronomical objects [[Zhar]], [[Farstine system|Farstine]],<ref name="TFABG" /> [[Tovash Tchii]],<ref name="Galaxy Map" /> and [[Enarc]].<ref name="TFABG" />

===Junctions===
The Triellus Trade Route crossed paths with a number of other hyperspace routes on its journey. At Centares, it intersected the [[Perlemian Trade Route]],<ref name="Galaxy Map" /> a [[super-hyperroute]]<ref name="BMF 48">{{BuildFalconCite|48|Guide to the Galaxy}}</ref> reaching to the [[Core Worlds]]. The route also intersected the<ref name="Galaxy Map" /> [[Salin Corridor]] at Sy Myrth,<ref name="SWT locations" /> the [[Pabol Sleheyron]] at Formos, and the [[Manda Merchant Route|Manda Merchant Run]] at Molavar.<ref name="RO locations" /> The Triellus Trade Route then had junctions with the [[Cloak of the Sith]] at Roon, the [[Mumble's Turnaround]] at Tatooine,<ref name="Smuggler's Guide" /> and [[the Crystal Passage]] at Geonosis.<ref name="BMF 19" /> At Arkanis, it crossed the [[Corellian Run]],<ref name="Galaxy Map" /> another super-hyperroute<ref name="BMF 48" /> which stretched to the Core Worlds.<ref name="Galaxy Map" /> Llanic saw the route intersect with the [[Llanic Spice Run]].<ref name="Heir" /> The Triellus Trade Route also briefly merged with the [[Darkknell–New Cov hyperlane]].<ref name="Map">{{StarWarsGalaxyMap}}</ref>

==History==
[[File:Spice-Triangle-SWSG.png|thumb|left|250px|The Triellus Trade Route formed part of the Spice Triangle trade network]]
By the time of the [[Clone Wars]] between the [[Galactic Republic]] and [[Confederacy of Independent Systems|Separatist Alliance]], the [[Hutt Clan]] controlled the Triellus Trade Route. When the Hutts allied with the Republic during the wars, the Separatists was unable to use the route to connect its [[Spinward/Canon|spinward]] and [[Trailing/Canon|trailing]] territories, leaving them especially vulnerable to siege.<ref name="Collapse" /> At some point by the [[Imperial Era|time]] of the [[Galactic Empire]], a trade network known as the [[Spice Triangle]] was formed, made up of Tatooine, Roon, and the planet [[Ryloth]] and controlled by the [[Pyke Syndicate]] as they began challenging Hutt territory. Linking the three worlds was the Triellus Trade Route, the Cloak of the Sith and the Corellian Run. The Triellus Trade Route notably made up the journey between Roon and Tatooine in the triangle.<ref name="Smuggler's Guide" />

Sometime by [[10 BBY]],<ref name="Date">The entry in ''[[Star Wars: Smuggler's Guide]]'' mentioning the the Triellus Trade Route is placed chronologically prior to an entry written by the criminal [[Tobias Beckett]]. ''[[Solo: A Star Wars Story]]'' depicts Beckett's [[death]] on the [[planet]] [[Savareen]], and ''[[Solo: A Star Wars Story The Official Guide]]'' dates the events on Savareen in the film to nine [[Standard year|years]] after the [[proclamation of the New Order]]. As ''[[Star Wars: Galactic Atlas]]'' dates the proclamation to [[19 BBY]], Beckett's death must occur in [[10 BBY]], and so his entry in the guide and those chronologically before it must all be set prior to or during 10 [['ABY-BBY' dating system|BBY]].</ref> the [[Volpai]] [[smuggler]] [[Tryphon Leo]] stole a [[book]] from the former [[pirate]] [[Queen]] [[Maz Kanata]], later known as the ''[[Smuggler's Guide]]'', which contained trade routes, [[shadowport]]s, criminal contacts and the location of her hidden treasure caches. With the book's information, Leo planned to loot one of the caches and set up a trade network with its wealth, which involved him locking down trade throughout the Spice Triangle. The planned lockdown involved tolls along the lucrative segments of the Triellus Trade Route, Leo believing a [[fleet]] of [[starship]]s and the bribing of powerful players in the area would allow him to make his changes. However, the smuggler's plans were stopped when he was crushed by a boulder trying to reach the first cache.<ref name="Smuggler's Guide" />

==Behind the scenes==
The Triellus Trade Route first appeared in the [[2015]] novel ''[[Heir to the Jedi]]'', written by [[Kevin Hearne]].<ref name="Heir" />

